  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This report lists federal contracts with periods of performance ending within the next 12 months and highlights large recompete opportunities through September 2027. The dataset shows total expiring contract value of $236B. NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC holds the single largest expiring contract position at $43.2B, followed by multiple THE BOEING COMPANY entries at $32B, $18.1B, and $7.5B. Lockheed Martin, Bell Boeing, and other major defense and professional services suppliers also appear in the top ten. Expirations cluster across quarters: $12.4B in Jul-Sep 2026, $45.2B in Oct-Dec 2026, $46.5B in Jan-Mar 2027, $83B in Apr-Jun 2027, and $49B in Jul-Sep 2027. Note: award value figures are total contract values for contracts whose period of performance ends within the next 12 months, not single-year obligations; end dates can be extended by options and modifications. Use this list to prioritize market outreach and capture planning for upcoming recompetes.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which contracts should capture teams prioritize?",
        "body": "NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC is the largest single expiring contract at $43.2B, making it a top priority for market and capture activity. THE BOEING COMPANY has multiple large expirations totaling $32B, $18.1B, and $7.5B that warrant focused business development. LOCKHEED MARTIN SERVICES, LLC at $20.6B and BELL BOEING JOINT PROJECT OFFICE at $7B round out high-value targets for defense and aerospace suppliers."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How are expirations distributed through the next 12 months?",
        "body": "Expiring contract value is concentrated in two quarters: $83B in Apr-Jun 2027 and $49B in Jul-Sep 2027. Earlier quarters include $12.4B in Jul-Sep 2026, $45.2B in Oct-Dec 2026, and $46.5B in Jan-Mar 2027. Total expiring contract value across all listed quarters is $236B."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Which large federal contracts are expiring soon?",
      "a": "Major contracts expiring include NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC with $43.2B, THE BOEING COMPANY with $32B, and LOCKHEED MARTIN SERVICES, LLC with $20.6B. Other top expiring contracts include THE BOEING COMPANY at $18.1B and $7.5B, BELL BOEING JOINT PROJECT OFFICE at $7B, CHEMONICS INTERNATIONAL, INC. at $6.7B, SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION at $6B, NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION at $5.4B, and BATH IRON WORKS CORPORATION at $5B."
    },
    {
      "q": "What is a contract recompete?",
      "a": "A contract recompete is the procurement event that follows a contract whose period of performance is ending, when agencies solicit offers to award a successor contract. Recompetes can include follow-on contracts, competitive award actions, or extensions through options and modifications."
    },
    {
      "q": "How current is this recompete data?",
      "a": "The period covered is FY2026 to date. The dataset reports award value figures for contracts whose period of performance ends within the next 12 months, and end dates can be extended by options and modifications."
    }
  ],
